{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the observational likelihood `y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma)` is unchanged and `y` remains the only protected data variable. The parameter priors were mechanically reorganized for SafeStan: `lambda ~ cauchy(0, 1)` was moved before any model-block use of `lambda`, and the loop of indexed prior statements for `theta_tilde[k]` was replaced by one vectorized top-level prior `theta_tilde ~ normal(0, theta_tilde_scale)` using a deterministic local scale vector. This preserves the same log density. No data fields were added; `data_safe.json` is the supplied data unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> K;                       // Number of groups
  int<lower=0> N;                       // Number of observations
  vector[N] y;                          // Observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> context_idx; // Context assignments

  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] w;        // Partial centering parameters

  real<lower=0> tau;                    // Base Population Scale
  real<lower=0> sigma;                  // Measurement variability
}

parameters {
  vector[K] theta_tilde;
  vector<lower=0>[K] lambda;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[K] theta;
  for (k in 1:K)
    theta[k] = pow(lambda[k] * tau, 1 - w[k]) * theta_tilde[k];
}

model {
  vector[K] theta_tilde_scale;

  lambda ~ cauchy(0, 1);

  for (k in 1:K)
    theta_tilde_scale[k] = pow(lambda[k] * tau, w[k]);
  theta_tilde ~ normal(0, theta_tilde_scale);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":4,"N":3,"context_idx":[2,2,2],"sigma":3.815486156116925,"tau":0.008514233953961182,"w":[0.423811761541048,0.10524988791937831,0.16780441501759616,0.3369114615062358],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
